DefinitionA prompt versioning system tracks and manages different versions of prompts so you can update, test, roll back, and compare them safely in production.Why it is usedAvoid breaking changes in promptsEnable A/B testingTrack improvements over timeRoll back to stable versions easilyHow it works (step-by-step)Store prompts with version IDs (v1, v2, etc.)Tag prompts with metadata (date, description)Retrieve prompt by versionUse selected version in LLM callsLog performance metrics per versionSwitch or roll back when neededKey componentsPrompt registry: Stores all versionsVersion ID: Unique identifier (v1, v2…)Metadata: Description, author, timestampSelector: Chooses active versionHistory tracking: Keeps changesBasic implementation (Python)import time

class PromptRegistry:
    def __init__(self):
        self.prompts = {}
        self.active_version = None

    def add_prompt(self, version, template, description=""):
        self.prompts[version] = {
            "template": template,
            "description": description,
            "created_at": time.time()
        }

    def set_active(self, version):
        if version not in self.prompts:
            raise ValueError("Version not found")
        self.active_version = version

    def get_prompt(self, version=None):
        version = version or self.active_version
        if version not in self.prompts:
            raise ValueError("Version not found")
        return self.prompts[version]["template"]

    def list_versions(self):
        return list(self.prompts.keys())

